    "user": "premathul",
    "created_at": "2026-11-18T04:29:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T04:29:34Z",
    "body": "Kunming, I agree this regional-energy comparison is a useful next step. The small change in stored-energy distribution is encouraging, while I agree that it does not establish convergence of the weak conversion or identify the source of its mesh sensitivity.\n\nWhat do you recommend as the next steps? Could the existing complex fields and channel amplitudes help distinguish numerical phase accumulation in the lead interiors from discretization error in the patterned region? The h100/h80 comparison changes both, so the regional energies alone do not locate the error.\n\nPlease indicate what the saved data can establish and what remains underdetermined. If a new calculation is needed, could you propose a bounded control and acceptance criterion for discussion first? Please retain the failed scattering gates and do not start another solve or refinement based on this comment."
  },
